# services/api — direct production dependencies (P8, D-22).
#
# The FastAPI read layer installs from this file's compiled lock (requirements-api.lock), NOT
# from the repository-wide requirements.lock. Reason, in full, in docs/decisions/
# D-22-split-api-dependency-manifest.md: the wide lock also carries vnstock and its mandatory
# closure (pandas, numpy, matplotlib, seaborn, wordcloud, pillow, openpyxl), none of which
# services/api imports, and a metered deployment build installs the whole thing on every push.
#
# THIS FILE MUST STAY IDENTICAL TO the `# --- API (services/api/app) ---` block in
# requirements.in. The two overlap by design and nothing checks the agreement — there is no CI.
# It is four lines and a strict subset, so the comparison is a glance, not a diff.
#
# Every entry traces to a real import in services/api/app: main.py (fastapi), the uvicorn ASGI
# server that runs it, config.py (pydantic-settings), db/connection.py and db/ping.py (psycopg2).
# Do NOT add a package that no API path imports, and do NOT add test/lint/notebook packages.
#
# Regenerate the lock authoritatively in a disposable Linux container — never on Windows, and
# never by hand-editing the pins. Same procedure and same pinned compiler as requirements.lock;
# the command is in that file's header, with requirements-api.in / requirements-api.lock
# substituted for the paths.

